      "widgets_values": [
        "**Angle:**\nFull-length fashion shot from a slight low three-quarter angle, subject captured mid-stride filling most of the frame with dynamic movement.\n\n**Pose:**\nYoung Japanese woman walking forward with left leg extended, right leg trailing, body gently twisted toward the camera, head turned slightly to her right with a soft natural gaze, left hand lightly holding the hem of her dress to create flowing motion while right hand carries a small turquoise bag by her side.\n\n**Subject:**\nYoung Japanese woman with brown eyes, natural skin texture showing fine pores and realistic subsurface scattering on arms and décolletage.\n\n**Outfit & Texture:**\nVibrant red sleeveless midi dress with a fitted bodice and voluminous multi-tiered ruffled skirt, lightweight cotton-poplin fabric with visible weave and natural drape creating dynamic folds and movement; single-strand pearl necklace resting on the collarbone; small structured turquoise handbag with short handle; delicate silver flat sandals with thin straps.\n\n**Background & Environment:**\nMinimalist studio interior with smooth neutral gray walls and light gray floor, clean architectural lines with soft shadow play, ample negative space emphasizing the subject.\n\n**Camera:**\n85mm lens, f/2.8, shallow depth of field with creamy bokeh in the background, sharp focus on the face and dress details, subtle motion blur on the moving skirt hem.\n\n**Lighting:**\nSoft diffused key light from the front-left at 4800K creating elegant modeling on the face and fabric, gentle fill from the right balancing shadows, clean rim lighting separating the red dress from the background with beautiful highlights on the ruffles.\n\n**Quality & Detail:**\nPhotorealistic fabric rendering with visible thread texture and natural creases in the red dress, dynamic skirt movement with realistic folds and flying ruffles, lustrous pearls with subtle reflections, smooth leather-like texture on the turquoise bag, fine skin details on arms and legs, high-fidelity color saturation and material distinction throughout."
      ]
